WEBVTT

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.190
Industrial threat hunting is a proactive,

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:05.230
defensive search for suspicious or unexplained activity.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:09.070
It differs from alert response by starting with a hypothesis rather than a generated

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:09.565
signal.

00:00:09.565 --> 00:00:14.265
It remains grounded in safety, reliability, process integrity, and operational authority.

00:00:14.265 --> 00:00:18.500
Effective hunts depend on asset inventory, real architecture, expected communication,

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:22.700
process modes, and telemetry from networks, protocols, identities, remote access,

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.305
endpoints, historians, and controller changes.

00:00:25.305 --> 00:00:28.905
Every source has blind spots, so confidence must match actual coverage.

00:00:28.905 --> 00:00:31.180
Useful hypotheses are focused and testable.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:35.255
Hunts may examine unauthorized access, abnormal industrial communication,

00:00:35.255 --> 00:00:37.515
or engineering and configuration activity.

00:00:37.515 --> 00:00:41.280
Observed anomalies are leads rather than proof; maintenance, faults, failover,

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.685
and legitimate work can produce similar evidence.

00:00:43.685 --> 00:00:48.440
Documentation preserves the plan, evidence, findings, confidence, operational explanation,

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.176
and follow-up.

00:00:49.176 --> 00:00:51.305
Repeatable findings can become detections,

00:00:51.305 --> 00:00:55.015
while inventory corrections and monitoring gaps improve the environment even when a

00:00:55.015 --> 00:00:56.585
hypothesis is not supported.

00:00:56.585 --> 00:01:00.435
The goal is not to disrupt production or perform offensive experimentation.

00:01:00.435 --> 00:01:03.785
It is better visibility, earlier detection, and safer operations.

00:01:03.785 --> 00:01:06.235
Security hunters provide investigative discipline;

00:01:06.235 --> 00:01:09.935
operators and engineers provide process meaning and safe response guidance.

00:01:09.935 --> 00:01:13.510
Their collaboration turns uncertain observations into defensible action.
